    <sys:String x:Key="GridUtility.BillsHeading">Utility bills</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="GridUtility.BillsIntro">Choose one way to start: importing the PDF fills this same review form; “New manual bill” leaves it blank. You do not need to use both methods. Either path creates the same bill record and preserves which facts were actually printed.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="GridUtility.BillEntryPdfTitle">Start from the PDF</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="GridUtility.BillEntryPdfIntro">Select the bill: the app preserves the original PDF and fills this same form with the facts it can read. You review everything before saving.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="GridUtility.BillEntryManualTitle">First-class manual entry</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="GridUtility.BillEntryManualIntro">If you prefer to transcribe it, open a clean form and copy only what appears on the bill. You can attach its PDF later without duplicating the bill.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="GridUtility.NewManualBill">New manual bill</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="GridUtility.BillPrimaryDataHeading">1. Printed readings, period and consumption</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="GridUtility.BillPrimaryDataIntro">Copy what you see on the bill. You do not need to enter these readings in another tab first: the printed numbers and billing dates go directly here.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="GridUtility.BillPrintedPreviousReading">Printed previous reading (kWh)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="GridUtility.BillPrintedCurrentReading">Printed current reading (kWh)</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="GridUtility.BillConsumptionHint">If both readings are entered, the app calculates their difference. If the bill also prints total consumption, it is used as a cross-check.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="GridUtility.BillTariffHint">Optional. Copy it only when printed; it is used to verify the applicable official tariff table, not to calculate consumption.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="GridUtility.BillConsumptionCheckIdle">Readings and consumption: enter what is printed and the app will check consistency.</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="GridUtility.BillFinancialHeading">2. Billing summary exactly as printed</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="GridUtility.BillFinancialIntro">These labels follow the Enel bill summary. Enter amounts with the printed sign; the app checks the arithmetic and never invents an adjustment to force a match.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="GridUtility.PreviousBalance">Previous balance</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="GridUtility.BillFinancialCheckIdle">Check: enter the printed amounts and the app will verify subtotal and total.</sys:String>

    <sys:String x:Key="GridUtility.BillIvaHint">Audit reference: Chilean standard VAT is 19%. The app reconstructs it only when a sufficient taxable base is available.</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="GridUtility.BillPdfPreviewHeading">3. Review evidence detected in the PDF</sys:String>
    <sys:String x:Key="GridUtility.BillPdfPreviewIntro">These lines are not canonical until the review is saved. Confirm descriptions and amounts against the document.</sys:String>
